cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this work, please cite it as below, together with the original paper by Thuerey et al. (2020)."
title: "Deep Flow Prediction on OpenFOAM v2606, extended to inverted airfoils in ground effect"
type: software
authors:
  - given-names: "Muhammad Taimoor Aslam"
    family-names: "Sial"
    orcid: "https://orcid.org/0009-0007-2268-1977"
repository-code: "https://github.com/taimooraslam22g/deep-flow-prediction-openfoam-v2606"
license: Apache-2.0
abstract: >-
  A reproduction of the U-Net of Thuerey et al. (AIAA Journal, 2020), which predicts
  RANS flow fields (pressure and velocity) around airfoils, on OpenFOAM v2606, gmsh 4
  and Docker, extended to inverted airfoils in ground effect (F1 front wings). It
  contains the ground-effect data generator (OpenFOAM, Spalart-Allmaras model, moving
  ground, boundary-layer mesh), its verification and validation (high-resolution LES of
  a NACA 4412, wind-tunnel tests of the Tyrrell 026 wing, grid convergence), the
  smoothing of 1,462 UIUC airfoils, a parameter scan of where steady RANS converges in
  ground effect, and the code that trains and tests the U-Net on the ground-effect data.
keywords:
  - computational fluid dynamics
  - RANS
  - OpenFOAM
  - deep learning
  - U-Net
  - surrogate model
  - airfoil
  - ground effect
  - Formula 1
references:
